<% content_for :title, 'Build specification' %>

<div class='w-full pb-10 space-y-6'>
  <div class='mt-4'>
    <div class='text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-slate-400'>
      Technical Reference Manual
    </div>
    <div class='mt-1 text-2xl font-heading text-deepnight-orange'>
      Subsector build Specification
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class='grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3'>
    <section class='min-w-0 lg:col-span-1'>
      <div class='text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-slate-400'>
        Sample specification
      </div>

      <div class='mt-2 rounded-2xl border border-slate-800/70 bg-slate-950/50 overflow-hidden'>
        <div class='flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-3 border-b border-slate-800/70'>
          <span class='identifier-sm text-slate-200'>YAML</span>
          <span class='text-xs text-slate-500 font-mono'>2-space indentation</span>
        </div>

        <pre class='p-4 text-sm font-mono text-slate-100 whitespace-pre overflow-auto leading-relaxed'><code>type: STANDARD
unusualChance: 4
defaultSI: 2
populated:
  type: full
  allegiance: IM
  minTechLevel: 2
  maxTechLevel: 10
  minPopulationCode: 3
  maxPopulationCode: 12
exclude:
  - x: 1
    y: 1
  - x: 2
    y: 3
required:
  - x: 4
    y: 7
systems:
  - x: 1
    y: 6
  - x: 8
    y: 10
    name: Muir Station
    primary:
      type: G2
      class: V
      companion:
        type: M7
        class: V
      bodies:
        - uwp: X301000-0
        - uwp: terrestrial
          orbit: habitable
        - uwp: Small Gas Giant</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Right: Documentation -->
    <section class='min-w-0 lg:col-span-2'>
      <div class='text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-slate-400'>
        Reference
      </div>

      <div class='mt-2 rounded-2xl border border-slate-800/70 bg-slate-950/50 p-5'>
        <p class='mt-3 text-slate-400'>The format of the specification file is YAML. Keep indentation at 2 spaces. YAML is picky about that.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 mb-2">Properties</p>

        <dl class='space-y-5 text-sm'>
          <div>
            <dt class='font-semibold text-slate-200'>type</dt>
            <dd class='mt-1 text-slate-300'>
              The subsector's star density type. Controls the per-hex probability that a star system is placed when not using
              <span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>systems</span>.
            </dd>

            <div class='mt-2 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/30 p-3'>
              <p class='text-xs text-slate-300 font-semibold mb-2'>Options</p>
              <ul class='text-xs text-slate-300 space-y-1'>
                <li><span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>DENSE</span> – 60%</li>
                <li><span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>STANDARD</span> – 50%</li>
                <li><span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>MODERATE</span> – 40%</li>
                <li><span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>LOW</span> – 30%</li>
                <li><span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>SPARSE</span> – 20%</li>
                <li><span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>MINIMAL</span> – 10%</li>
                <li><span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>RIFT</span> – 3%</li>
                <li><span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>RIFT_FADE</span> – 2%</li>
                <li><span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>DEEP_RIFT</span> – 1%</li>
                <li><span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>EMPTY</span> – 0%</li>
              </ul>
              <p class='mt-2 text-xs text-slate-400'>
                Example: <span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>type: STANDARD</span>
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <dt class='font-semibold text-slate-200'>unusualChance</dt>
            <dd class='mt-1 text-slate-300'>
              Percentage chance that an ‘unusual’ result overrides normal generation for a system.
              Higher means stranger subsector outcomes.
            </dd>
          </div>

          <div>
            <dt class='font-semibold text-slate-200'>defaultSI</dt>
            <dd class='mt-1 text-slate-300'>
              Default Survey Index used when a system does not specify one explicitly. If not specified, defaults to 0.
            </dd>
          </div>

          <div>
            <dt class='font-semibold text-slate-200'>exclude</dt>
            <dd class='mt-1 text-slate-300'>
              List of subsector hex coordinates (x:1..8, y:1..10) where the generator must
              <span class='font-semibold text-slate-200'>not</span> place a star system.
            </dd>
          </div>

          <div>
            <dt class='font-semibold text-slate-200'>required</dt>
            <dd class='mt-1 text-slate-300'>
              List of hex coordinates that must <span class='font-semibold text-slate-200'>always</span> have a star system.
              A hex cannot appear in both <span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>required</span> and
              <span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>exclude</span>.
            </dd>
          </div>

          <div>
            <dt class='font-semibold text-slate-200'>systems</dt>
            <dd class='mt-1 text-slate-300'>
              If present and non-empty, the generator will place star systems
              <span class='font-semibold text-slate-200'>only</span> in these hexes. Only hex addresses included in
              the list will have star systems. In this mode, <span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>exclude</span> and
              <span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>required</span> are ignored.
            </dd>

            <div class='mt-2 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/30 p-3'>
              <p class='text-xs text-slate-300 font-semibold mb-2'>Example behaviour</p>
              <p class='text-xs text-slate-300'>
                When <span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>systems</span> is set, only those hexes get systems. Nothing else does.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <dt class='font-semibold text-slate-200'>populated</dt>
            <dd class='mt-1 text-slate-300'>
              Optional defaults for population generation (applies to systems created by the build).
            </dd>
            <div class='mt-2 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/30 p-3'>
              <ul class='text-xs text-slate-300 space-y-1'>
                <li><span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>type</span> – layout preset for how populated worlds are distributed</li>
                <li><span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>allegiance</span> – default allegiance code</li>
                <li><span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>minTechLevel</span>, <span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>maxTechLevel</span></li>
                <li><span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>minPopulationCode</span>, <span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>maxPopulationCode</span></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <dt class='font-semibold text-slate-200'>primary</dt>
            <dd class='mt-1 text-slate-300'>
              Optional star data for a specific system when using <span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>systems</span>.
              Star <span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>type</span> is spectral class + subtype (OBAFGKM + 0–9), like
              <span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>G2</span>. Star <span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>class</span> is luminosity class (V, IV, III, etc.).
            </dd>
          </div>

          <div>
            <dt class='font-semibold text-slate-200'>bodies</dt>
            <dd class='mt-1 text-slate-300'>
              Optional list of bodies. Each body requires <span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>uwp</span> and may include
              <span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>orbit</span> which must be one of
              <span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>habitable</span>, <span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>warm</span>, or
              <span class='font-mono text-slate-200'>cold</span>.
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
